## Resource gate (ACTIVE / MANDATORY; thresholds unchanged)

Minimum observation: **≥5 minutes**, ≥5 samples, ~60 seconds apart.
For ~60-second spacing, collect enough samples to prove first-to-last span
**≥300 seconds**.

Reject if **any** of:

- swap-out (`so`) > 0 on a majority of samples
- **median** data-device (`dm-0`) `%util` ≥ 80 **AND** median iowait ≥ 10
- **any two consecutive** samples with dm-0 `%util` ≥ 95 **AND** iowait ≥ 10

One favorable sample must not override a bad observation window.
Do not weaken these thresholds.

## Next Owner gate

**C2 POST-PAUSE IO BLOCKER RCA**

This gate may authorize read-only production investigation,
process/device/DB attribution, query/IO correlation, an RCA evidence packet,
and candidate remediation design.

Read-only RCA should at minimum investigate:

- PostgreSQL IO independent of the collector
- currently active query families after collector-removal evidence
- telegram_messages and other high-IO relations
- buffer/cache miss pressure
- checkpoint / background writer / WAL pressure
- autovacuum/vacuum/analyze state
- swap pressure / memory reclaim
- filesystem/device queueing and latency
- other TitanGold processes
- non-TitanGold host processes if material
- unexplained telegram_messages SELECTs without application_name
- whether MAX(message_id) remains material when collector is not the source
- whether host/device saturation is driven by another workload
- whether a safe time-window change alone could solve the gate
- whether a technical remediation is required before 052

RCA is read-only discovery unless a later exact Owner task authorizes a fix.

This gate does **not** authorize:

052, capsule DB connection, CREATE/DROP INDEX, VACUUM/ANALYZE,
query cancellation, process kill/restart, PM2 mutation, OS tuning,
swap mutation, DB config mutation, pgmigrations, 050, or 051.
